# Request and response

## Framework semantics

Controllers receive `ServerRequest` and return `Response` (or use `render`/`redirect`). Flash messages use Flash component/helper. Prefer PSR-7 style request data access over `$_POST`/`$_GET`.

## Required behavior

- Read input via `$this->request` / `$request->getData()` / `getQuery()` / `getParam()`.
- Set status codes, headers, and cookies on the response deliberately.
- Use Flash for user feedback the project’s way; do not invent session flash schemas.
- Avoid open redirects — only redirect to known-safe local paths/routes.
- Do not invent Laravel Request facades / FormRequest.

## Anti-patterns

- Reading `$_POST`/`$_GET` directly in new CakePHP code
- Open redirects from unvalidated user-supplied URLs
- Fat responses that embed persistence logic

## Review checklist

- [ ] Input via request APIs
- [ ] Redirects are safe
- [ ] Flash usage matches neighbors
